 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## Authentication and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`.
+
+- `viewer` may only read (GET).
+- `cook` may also cook recipes (`POST /recipes/:id/cook`), record waste
+  (`POST /batches/:id/waste`), log temperatures (`POST /temperatures`) and
+  enter stock-take counts (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager` may do everything.
+
+A missing or unknown key is 401 `unauthorized`; a known key without
+permission is 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request by a known key that is not a GET appends an entry
+`{ at, keyName, method, path, status }` to `audit` in the data (the status
+is the one answered, including errors). `GET /audit` lists them newest first
+(managers only).
